te\": \"C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 \u00b5F/25 V\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(comp (ref \\\"C1\\\") (value \\\"0.1uF/16V\\\")\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"The bulk decoupling on the display power rail is about ten times smaller than specified, which could degrade the boost and display supply stability.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.35\n    },\n    {\n      \"category\": \"wrong_value\",\n      \"components\": [\"BAT+ source (V_BAT_)\"],\n      \"pins\": [],\n      \"nets\": [\"BAT+\"],\n      \"observed\": \"The SPICE deck drives the BAT+ net with a 25.0 V DC source. The netlist shows BAT+ as the battery-derived rail feeding the FAN53610 VIN pin.\",\n      \"expected\": \"A single 18650 Li-ion cell (spec \u00a71 and \u00a73) is roughly 3.0\u20134.2 V. A 25 V source is far outside the FAN53610 VIN rating of about 5.5 V.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"spice\", \"quote\": \"V_BAT_ BAT+ 0 DC 25.0\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"single-cell Li-ion battery holder\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"If this simulation stimulus reflects the intended supply, the regulator and capacitors would be overstressed. As a simulation artifact it would make the SPICE results invalid for the board.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.25\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The netlist is largely consistent with the specification, but C11 carries an inductor footprint on a floating capacitor, and C1's value (0.1 uF/16 V) departs from the spec's stated 1 uF/25 V. The SPICE battery source of 25 V is also implausible for a single 18650 cell.\"\n}",
